From 5b257aa02094dd2ed3148a8feef481e43e07ff9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 01:36:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/20] avcodec/ppc: add AltiVec-optimized VP9 decoder

Ported from the platform-uxp (Firefox ffvpx) tree, which carries this
as a from-scratch AltiVec implementation for the mozavcodec build:
https://github.com/Jazzzny/platform-uxp/commit/8d02131b2a106e511489901613ed642b4951b8e9

Adapted to build under the standard FFmpeg build system (CONFIG_VP9_DECODER
Makefile rule and ff_vp9dsp_init_ppc arch dispatch) instead of moz.build;
the DSP code itself is unchanged, as the VP9DSPContext layout and helper
macros already matched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KpUsGMxFgGTrTWRfW8PB8S
